illas_option_use-even-on-capital-letters_example":"Contoh: États-Unis; Ça va ?; Façonné","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-and-cedillas_option_use-even-on-capital-letters_name":"Gunakan tanda diakritik dan cedilla, bahkan pada huruf kapital.","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-and-cedillas_option_never-use_example":"Contoh: Etats-Unis; Ca va ?; Faconne","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-and-cedillas_option_never-use_name":"Jangan pernah menggunakan tanda diakritik atau cedilla.","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-and-cedillas_option_do-not-use-on-capital-letters_name":"Gunakan tanda diakritik dan cedilla, kecuali pada huruf kapital.","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_compound-nouns_name":"Menulis kata majemuk","item_form_field_zh_spelling-and-grammar-v2_abbreviation-usage_name":"Singkatan","item_form_field_ko_spelling-and-grammar-v2_abbreviation-usage_option_use-abbreviations-as-needed_example":"Contoh: 노동조합(O) → 노조(O)","item_form_field_ko_spelling-and-grammar-v2_abbreviation-usage_option_use-abbreviations-as-needed_name":"Gunakan singkatan sesuai kebutuhan.","item_form_field_ko_spelling-and-grammar-v2_abbreviation-usage_option_do-not-use-abbreviations-unless-necessary_name":"Jangan gunakan singkatan kecuali jika diperlukan.","item_form_field_zh_spelling-and-grammar-v2_abbreviation-usage_option_do-not-use-abbreviations_name":"Jangan gunakan singkatan","item_form_field_zh_spelling-and-grammar-v2_foreign-word-translation_name":"Menerjemahkan kata-kata asing","item_form_field_zh_spelling-and-grammar-v2_abbreviation-usage_option_use-abbreviations_name":"Gunakan singkatan","item_form_field_it_spelling-and-grammar-v2_all-caps_example":"Contoh: CISL, UIL e UGL sono tre confederazioni sindacali italiane","item_form_field_es_spelling-and-grammar-v2_all-caps_example":"Contoh: ONU; AVE","item_form_field_es_spelling-and-grammar-v2_all-caps_name":"Jangan menulis kata-kata atau teks lengkap dengan huruf kapital, kecuali untuk singkatan atau nama merek tertentu.","item_form_field_it_spelling-and-grammar-v2_all-caps_name":"Jangan gunakan huruf kapital semua, kecuali saat menulis akronim, inisial, atau kata benda yang tepat.","item_form_field_it_spelling-and-grammar-v2_active-passive-voice_name":"Gunakan kalimat aktif. Gunakan kalimat pasif hanya jika pelaku tidak diketahui atau tidak relevan.","item_form_field_ja_spelling-and-grammar-v2_active-passive-voice_option_use-passive-voice-for-automatic-operations-from-user-perspective_example":"Contoh: Data dikirimkan","item_form_field_ja_spelling-and-grammar-v2_active-passive-voice_option_use-passive-voice-for-automatic-operations-from-user-perspective_name":"Ketika operasi dilakukan secara otomatis dari sudut pandang pengguna, gunakan kalimat pasif.","item_form_field_ko_spelling-and-grammar-v2_active-passive-voice_option_use-passive-voice-as-needed_name":"Gunakan kalimat pasif sesuai kebutuhan.","item_form_field_ja_spelling-and-grammar-v2_active-passive-voice_option_use-active-voice-to-describe-operations-with-user-as-subject_name":"Saat menjelaskan operasi, gunakan kalimat aktif dengan pengguna sebagai subjek untuk menyatukan sudut pandang.","item_form_field_zh_spelling-and-grammar-v2_active-passive-voice_option_use-active-voice-if-subject-is-prominent-and-agent-is-clear_name":"Gunakan kalimat aktif ketika subjeknya menonjol dan pelakunya jelas.","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-in-verbs-conjugated-like-french-word-céder_name":"Menuliskan kata kerja yang berkonjugasi seperti “céder” dalam bentuk masa depan dan mood kondisional.","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-in-verbs-conjugated-like-french-word-céder_option_use-acute-accent_example":"Contoh: je considérerai","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-with-subject-verb-inversion_option_use-acute-accent_example":"Contoh: aimé-je","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-with-subject-verb-inversion_option_use-grave-accent_example":"Contoh: aimè-je","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-with-subject-verb-inversion_option_use-grave-accent_name":"Gunakan tanda diakritik grave (ejaan yang diperbarui)","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-with-subject-verb-inversion_option_use-acute-accent_name":"Gunakan tanda diakritik akut (penulisan tradisional)","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-with-subject-verb-inversion_name":"Menekankan kata kerja ketika subjek dan kata kerja dibalik","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-in-verbs-conjugated-like-french-word-céder_option_use-grave-accent_example":"Contoh: je considèrerai","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-in-verbs-conjugated-like-french-word-céder_option_use-grave-accent_name":"Gunakan tanda diakritik grave (ejaan yang diperbarui)","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_conjunctions_name":"Jangan pernah memulai kalimat dengan kata sambung koordinatif.","item_form_field_fr_spelling-and-grammar-v2_accents-in-verbs-conjugated-like-french-word-céder_option_use-acute-accent_name":"Gunakan tanda diakritik akut (penulisan tradisional)","item_form_field_ko_spelling-and-grammar-v2_active-passive-voice_option_use-active-voice-unless-agent-is-unknown-or-irrelevant_name":"Gunakan kalimat aktif; gunakan kalimat pasif hanya jika pelaku tidak diketahui atau tidak relevan.","item_form_field_zh_spelling-and-grammar-v2_active-passive-voice_option_use-passive-voice-if-agent-is-unknown-or-irrelevant_name":"Gunakan kalimat pasif ketika pelaku tidak diketahui atau tidak relevan.","item_form_field_ko_spelling-and-grammar-v2_established-loanwords_name":"Kata serapan yang telah mapan","item_form_field_ko_spelling-and-grammar-v2_abbreviation-usage_name":"Penggunaan singkatan","item_form_field_en_spelling-and-grammar-v2_contractions_option_use-contractions-but-avoid-negative-contractions_name":"Gunakan, tetapi hindari kontraksi negatif","item_form_field_en_spelling-and-grammar-v2_latin-abbreviations_name":"Jangan gunakan singkatan Latin, seperti i.e., ibid., atau etc.","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_ellipsis_option_use-ellipsis-character_example":"Contoh: …","item_form_field_fr_punctuation-v2_ellipsis_option_use-ellipsis-character_example":"Contoh: À suivre…","item_form_field_fr_punctuation-v2_ellipsis_option_use-ellipsis-character_name":"Gunakan karakter titik tiga (…)","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_ellipsis_option_use-three-spaced-periods_example":"Contoh: . . .","item_form_field_fr_punctuation-v2_ellipsis_option_use-three-periods_example":"Contoh: À suivre…","item_form_field_fr_punctuation-v2_ellipsis_option_use-three-periods_name":"Gunakan tiga titik (...)","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_ellipsis_option_use-three-spaced-periods_name":"Gunakan tiga titik yang dipisahkan oleh spasi.","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_ellipsis_option_use-ellipsis-character_name":"Gunakan karakter elipsis","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_ellipsis_option_use-one-ellipsis-character_name":"Gunakan satu titik tiga (“…”)","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_ellipsis_option_use-three-ellipsis-characters_name":"Gunakan tiga titik tiga (\"………\")","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_ellipsis_option_use-two-ellipsis-characters_name":"Gunakan dua titik tiga (“……”)","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_salutation_option_use-colon-after-salutation_example":"Contoh: Dear Mr. Smith:","item_form_field_es_punctuation-v2_salutation_option_use-colon-after-salutation_example":"Contoh: Buenos días:","item_form_field_es_punctuation-v2_salutation_option_use-colon-after-salutation_name":"Gunakan tanda titik dua (standar yang direkomendasikan)","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_salutation_option_use-comma-after-salutation_example":"Contoh: Dear John,","item_form_field_es_punctuation-v2_salutation_option_use-comma-after-salutation_example":"Contoh: Buenos días,","item_form_field_es_punctuation-v2_salutation_option_use-comma-after-salutation_name":"Gunakan koma","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_salutation_option_use-comma-after-salutation_name":"Gunakan koma (informal)","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_salutation_option_use-colon-after-salutation_name":"Gunakan tanda titik dua (formal)","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_quotation-style_option_use-single-quotation-marks-for-primary-quotations-and-double-quotation-marks-for-secondary-quotations_example":"Contoh: ‘The first chapter of the UN Charter “Purposes and Principles” is crucial’, said the professor.","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_passage-of-time-and-movement-between-locations_example":"Contoh:\n5分——10分——15分;\n電車が、静岡——浜松——名古屋と進んでいった","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_passage-of-time-and-movement-between-locations_name":"Saat menunjukkan berlalunya waktu atau pergerakan antara lokasi, gunakan tanda hubung ganda.","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_full-sentence-in-round-brackets_example":"Contoh: 今年の生産量は10tだった。（昨年は8tだった。）","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_full-sentence-in-round-brackets_name":"Ketika tanda kurung bulat mengapit kalimat lengkap, tambahkan titik Jepang pada kalimat tersebut.","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_round-brackets_name":"Kurung bulat","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_periods-in-uppercase-initialisms-and-acronyms_name":"Jangan gunakan titik untuk singkatan huruf besar.","item_form_field_it_punctuation-v2_uppercase-acronyms_name":"Saat menulis akronim huruf besar","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_periods-and-commas_name":"Titik dan koma","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_quotation-style_option_use-single-quotation-marks-for-primary-quotations-and-double-quotation-marks-for-secondary-quotations_name":"Tanda kutip tunggal untuk kutipan utama dan tanda kutip ganda untuk kutipan sekunder (Bahasa Inggris Britania)","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_text-in-round-brackets-referring-to-previous-sentence_name":"Teks dalam kurung bulat mengubah seluruh kalimat.","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_text-in-round-brackets-referring-to-previous-sentence_option_add-period-after-closing-round-bracket_example":"Contoh: Hari ini saya berjalan kaki ke luar (kemarin saya berlari ke luar).","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_text-in-round-brackets-supplementing-preceding-text_example":"Contoh: Hari ini saya pergi berjalan kaki (bersama kakak).","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_text-in-round-brackets-supplementing-preceding-text_name":"Ketika teks dalam kurung bulat melengkapi teks sebelumnya, tambahkan titik Jepang setelah kurung bulat penutup.","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_text-in-round-brackets-referring-to-previous-sentence_option_add-period-before-closing-round-bracket_example":"Contoh: 今日は歩いて出かけた。（昨日は走って出かけた。）","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_text-in-round-brackets-referring-to-previous-sentence_option_add-period-before-closing-round-bracket_name":"Tambahkan titik sebelum kurung tutup.","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_text-in-round-brackets-referring-to-previous-sentence_option_add-period-after-closing-round-bracket_name":"Tambahkan titik setelah kurung bulat penutup.","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_setting-off-non-quoted-phrases_name":"Untuk menandai frasa penghubung selain kutipan","item_form_section_style-tone_name":"Gaya dan nada penulisan","item_form_section_punctuation_subsection_quotation-marks_name":"Tanda kutip","item_form_section_dates-times_subsection_date-format_name":"Format tanggal","item_form_section_dates-times_subsection_time-format_name":"Format waktu","item_form_field_en_style-and-tone-v2_idioms-colloquialisms-and-culture-specific-references_name":"Jangan gunakan idiom, bahasa sehari-hari, atau kata atau frasa yang khusus untuk budaya tertentu.","item_form_field_en_style-and-tone-v2_default-third-person-singular-pronoun_name":"Kata ganti gender","item_form_field_ko_style-and-tone-v2_default-first-person-pronoun_name":"Kata ganti orang pertama","item_form_field_en_style-and-tone-v2_default-third-person-singular-pronoun_option_use-he-him_example":"Contoh: The new CEO is in the office today. Let’s welcome him.","item_form_field_en_style-and-tone-v2_default-third-person-singular-pronoun_option_use-he-or-she-him-or-her_example":"Contoh: The new CEO is in the office today. Let’s welcome him or her.","item_form_field_es_style-and-tone-v2_addressing-non-binary-people_option_use-spanish-word-elle_example":"Contoh: elle es licenciade; elles son mis amigues; le amigue de mi compañera vive cerca","item_form_field_es_style-and-tone-v2_addressing-non-binary-people_option_use-spanish-word-ellx_example":"Contoh: ellx es licenciadx; ellxs son mis amigxs; lx amigx de mi compañera vive cerca","item_form_field_es_style-and-tone-v2_addressing-non-binary-people_option_use-spanish-word-ellx_name":"Gunakan bentuk inklusif “elix(s)”","item_form_field_es_style-and-tone-v2_addressing-non-binary-people_option_use-spanish-word-elle_name":"Gunakan bentuk inklusif “elle(s)”","item_form_field_it_style-and-tone-v2_referring-to-non-binary-people_example":"Contoh: Ləi è laureatə; Loro sono laureatɜ; Ti presento lə miə amicə; Loro sono lɜ miɜ amicɜ","item_form_field_it_style-and-tone-v2_referring-to-non-binary-people_name":"Saat merujuk pada orang nonbiner, gunakan akhiran schwa (“ə”) untuk bentuk tunggal dan akhiran schwa (“ɜ”) untuk bentuk jamak. Sebutan “ləi” untuk bentuk tunggal dan “loro” untuk bentuk jamak.","item_form_field_es_style-and-tone-v2_addressing-non-binary-people_name":"Ketika merujuk pada seseorang dengan identitas gender non-biner","search_noResults_customRules_headline":"Kami tidak dapat menemukan daftar aturan gaya dengan \"{{searchTerm}}.\"","item_form_field_en_style-and-tone-v2_default-third-person-singular-pronoun_option_use-they-them_example":"Contoh: The new CEO is in the office today. Let’s welcome them.","item_form_field_en_style-and-tone-v2_default-third-person-singular-pronoun_option_use-they-them_name":"Gunakan \"they/them” sebagai kata ganti orang ketiga tunggal default ketika jenis kelamin tidak ditentukan atau tidak relevan.","item_form_field_en_style-and-tone-v2_default-third-person-singular-pronoun_option_use-she-her_example":"Contoh: The new CEO is in the office today. Let’s welcome her.","item_form_field_en_style-and-tone-v2_default-third-person-singular-pronoun_option_use-he-or-she-him-or-her_name":"Gunakan \"he or she\" dan \"him or her\" daripada kata ganti tunggal ketika jenis kelamin tidak ditentukan atau tidak relevan.","item_form_field_ko_style-and-tone-v2_default-first-person-pronoun_option_do-not-use-first-person-pronouns_name":"Jangan gunakan kata ganti orang pertama untuk bentuk yang lebih netral.","item_form_field_ko_style-and-tone-v2_default-second-person-pronoun_option_do-not-use-second-person-pronouns_example":"Contoh: Pembaca; Pengguna; Pelanggan; Guru, dll.","item_form_field_zh_style-and-tone-v2_double-negatives_option_do-not-use-double-negatives_example":"没有人不觉得这个方案有问题。(“Tidak ada yang tidak berpikir bahwa tidak ada yang salah dengan paket langganan ini”);\nArti tersirat dari “大家都觉得有问题” (“Everyone thinks there is a problem”), but it could be misunderstood as “没人觉得有问题” (“No one thinks there is a problem”); sebaiknya diubah menjadi ungkapan langsung: “大家都觉得这个方案有问题。“(‘Semua orang berpikir ada yang salah dengan paket langganan ini.’)”","item_form_field_zh_style-and-tone-v2_double-negatives_option_use-double-negatives_example":"Contoh: 他的建议并非没有道理，我们可以考虑一下。\n“并非没有道理” (“It is not without reason”) = “有一定道理” (“It makes sense”), tetapi lebih halus karena menghindari afirmasi langsung","item_form_field_zh_style-and-tone-v2_double-negatives_option_do-not-use-double-negatives_name":"Hindari penggunaan kalimat negatif ganda untuk menghindari ambiguitas atau kesalahpahaman, atau ketika tidak perlu memperkuat bentuk.","item_form_field_zh_style-and-tone-v2_double-negatives_option_use-double-negatives_name":"Gunakan kalimat negatif ganda untuk memperkuat bentuk atau mengekspresikan afirmasi yang sopan atau tersirat.","item_form_field_ko_style-and-tone-v2_default-second-person-pronoun_option_do-not-use-second-person-pronouns_name":"Jangan gunakan kata ganti orang kedua untuk bentuk yang lebih netral.","item_form_field_ko_style-and-tone-v2_default-second-person-pronoun_option_use-second-person-pronouns_name":"Gunakan kata ganti orang kedua sebagaimana adanya.","item_form_field_ko_style-and-tone-v2_default-second-person-pronoun_name":"Kata ganti orang kedua","item_form_field_ko_style-and-tone-v2_default-first-person-pronoun_option_use-first-person-pronouns_name":"Gunakan kata ganti orang pertama sebagaimana adanya.","item_form_field_ko_style-and-tone-v2_default-first-person-pronoun_option_omit-first-person-subject-when-clear-from-context_name":"Hapus subjek orang pertama jika sudah jelas dari konteks.","item_form_section_style-tone_subsection_inclusive-language_name":"Bahasa yang inklusif","item_form_section_style-tone_subsection_word-choice_name":"Pemilihan kata","item_form_field_en_style-and-tone-v2_default-third-person-singular-pronoun_option_use-she-her_name":"Gunakan \"she/her\" sebagai kata ganti orang ketiga tunggal default ketika jenis kelamin tidak ditentukan atau tidak relevan.","item_form_field_en_style-and-tone-v2_default-third-person-singular-pronoun_option_use-he-him_name":"Gunakan \"he/him\" sebagai kata ganti orang ketiga tunggal default ketika jenis kelamin tidak ditentukan atau tidak relevan.","item_form_field_en_style-and-tone-v2_personal-vs-impersonal-style_name":"Bentuk pribadi atau impersonal","item_form_field_en_style-and-tone-v2_instructions-style_name":"Saat menulis instruksi, gunakan kalimat imperatif.","item_form_field_en_spelling-and-grammar-v2_contractions_name":"Kontraksi","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_ellipsis_name":"Untuk elipsis","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_salutation_name":"Setelah ucapan salam","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_quotation-style_option_use-double-quotation-marks-for-primary-quotations-and-single-quotation-marks-for-secondary-quotations_name":"Gunakan tanda kutip ganda untuk kutipan utama dan tanda kutip tunggal untuk kutipan sekunder (Bahasa Inggris Amerika)","item_form_field_ja_style-and-tone-v2_tone_option_use-dearu-style-to-give-impression-content-is-accurate-and-rigorous-or-to-convey-sense-of-confidence-and-reliability_name":"Gunakan gaya \"dearu\" ketika Anda ingin memberikan kesan bahwa konten tersebut akurat dan teliti, atau ketika Anda ingin menyampaikan rasa percaya diri dan keandalan.","style-tone_avoidingTechnicalJargon_description":"Gunakan kata-kata umum yang sering digunakan sehari-hari. Gunakan istilah teknis hanya jika benar-benar diperlukan.","style-tone_explainingTechnicalJargon_description":"Tambahkan penjelasan singkat mengenai istilah-istilah teknis yang digunakan dalam teks dan kemungkinan besar tidak akan dipahami oleh pembaca umum. Penjelasannya sebaiknya tidak lebih dari satu kalimat.","style-tone_explainingTechnicalJargon_title":"Menjelaskan istilah-istilah teknis","style-tone_avoidingTechnicalJargon_title":"Menghindari istilah-istilah teknis","item_form_field_zh_style-and-tone-v2_formality_name":"Formalitas","item_form_field_it_style-and-tone-v2_addressing-the-reader_option_use-formal-italian-word-lei_name":"Gunakan bentuk formal “lei”","item_form_field_fr_style-and-tone-v2_addressing-the-reader_name":"Menyampaikan pesan kepada pembaca","item_form_field_it_style-and-tone-v2_addressing-the-reader_option_use-informal-italian-word-tu_name":"Gunakan bentuk informal \"tu\"","item_form_field_fr_style-and-tone-v2_addressing-the-reader_option_use-formal-french-word-vous_name":"Gunakan \"vous\"","item_form_field_fr_style-and-tone-v2_anglicisms_name":"Hindari penggunaan kata-kata Inggris ketika ada padanan kata Prancis yang umum digunakan.","item_form_field_fr_style-and-tone-v2_addressing-the-reader_option_use-informal-french-word-tu_name":"Gunakan \"tu\"","item_form_field_ja_style-and-tone-v2_tone_option_use-desu-masu-style-to-give-impression-content-is-plain-and-straightforward-or-to-give-reader-reassuring-or-soft-impression_name":"Gunakan gaya \"desu/masu\" ketika Anda ingin memberikan kesan bahwa kontennya sederhana dan lugas, atau ketika Anda ingin memberikan kesan yang menenangkan atau lembut kepada pembaca.","style-tone_formalPoliteTone_description":"Gunakan nada bicara formal dan bentuk sopan dalam setiap kalimat.","style-tone_formalPoliteTone_title":"Gaya bahasa formal/bentuk sopan","style-tone_vividDescriptiveLanguage_description":"Teks harus menggunakan bahasa yang deskriptif dan hidup, sehingga mampu membangkitkan gambaran yang jelas dalam benak pembaca sebisa mungkin.","style-tone_vividDescriptiveLanguage_title":"Bahasa yang hidup dan deskriptif","item_form_field_zh_style-and-tone-v2_double-negatives_name":"Kalimat negatif ganda","item_form_field_ko_style-and-tone-v2_declarative-endings_name":"Akhiran deklaratif","item_form_field_it_style-and-tone-v2_gender-unspecified-or-mixed_name":"Ketika gender tidak ditentukan dan ketika merujuk pada kelompok yang terdiri dari orang-orang dengan gender campuran.","item_form_field_fr_style-and-tone-v2_gender-unspecified_name":"Ketika jenis kelamin satu atau lebih individual tidak ditentukan.","item_form_field_es_style-and-tone-v2_gender-unspecified-or-mixed_name":"Jika jenis kelamin suatu kelompok tidak ditentukan atau campuran","item_form_field_it_style-and-tone-v2_addressing-the-reader_name":"Ketika berbicara kepada pembaca","item_form_section_formatting_name":"Pengkodean","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_slash-usage_name":"Jangan gunakan tanda slash (/) untuk berarti \"or\"","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_sentence-break-indicator_name":"Tanda hubung panjang (—) atau tanda hubung pendek (–)","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_quotation-mark-and-apostrophe_option_use-straight-quotation-marks-and-apostrophes_example":"Contoh: \"The king's hat\"","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_quotation-mark-and-apostrophe_option_use-straight-quotation-marks-and-apostrophes_name":"Lurus","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_quotation-mark-and-apostrophe_option_use-curly-quotation-marks-and-apostrophes_name":"Keriting","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_quotation-style_name":"Tanda petik ganda atau tanda petik tunggal","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_comma-after-short-introductory-phrase_option_do-not-use_example":"Contoh: At work employees are required to wear safety gear.","item_form_field_ko_punctuation-v2_comma-after-conjunctive-adverbs_option_do-not-use_example":"Contoh: 그런데 나는...","item_form_field_ko_punctuation-v2_comma-after-conjunctive-adverbs_option_use_example":"Contoh: 그런데, 나는...","item_form_field_ko_punctuation-v2_comma-after-conjunctive-adverbs_option_do-not-use_name":"Jangan gunakan","item_form_field_ko_punctuation-v2_comma-after-conjunctive-adverbs_option_use_name":"Gunakan","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_comma-after-short-introductory-phrase_option_use_example":"Contoh: At work, employees are required to wear safety gear.","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_comma-after-short-introductory-phrase_option_do-not-use_name":"Jangan gunakan koma","item_form_field_en_style-and-tone-v2_redundant-introductory-phrases_name":"Jangan gunakan frasa yang merujuk pada teks yang sudah ada jika penggunaannya akan menjadi berlebihan.","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_quotation-mark-and-apostrophe_name":"Tanda kutip melengkung atau lurus dan tanda apostrof","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_comma-after-short-introductory-phrase_option_use_name":"Gunakan koma","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_ampersand-usage_example":"Contoh: We’re increasing the budget for multiple departments, including R&D and Sales.","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_ampersand-usage_name":"Ganti & dengan “and”, kecuali dalam nama perusahaan, singkatan umum, gelar, kode perangkat lunak, dan persamaan matematika.","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_ampersand-usage_name":"Ampersand","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_ampersand-abbreviation-spacing_option_use-spaces-before-and-after-ampersand-as-part-of-abbreviation_example":"Contoh: R & D; M & A","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_ampersand-abbreviation-spacing_option_do-not-use-spaces-before-and-after-ampersand-as-part-of-abbreviation_name":"Jangan gunakan spasi","item_form_field_zh_formatting-v2_paragraph-spacing_option_do-not-place-blank-line-between-paragraphs_name":"Jangan menambah baris kosong di antara paragraf.","item_form_field_zh_formatting-v2_paragraph-spacing_option_place-blank-line-between-paragraphs_name":"Tambahkan baris kosong di antara paragraf.","item_form_field_ja_punctuation-v2_japanese-reference-materials_name":"Gunakan tanda kurung sudut ganda untuk materi referensi yang ditulis dalam bahasa Jepang.","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_range-indicator_name":"Saat menunjukkan rentang angka atau tanggal","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_possessives-of-proper-names-ending-in-s-style_name":"Ketika membentuk bentuk kepemilikan untuk kata benda sendiri yang berakhiran “s”","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_possessives-of-proper-names-ending-in-s-style_option_add-apostrophe-only_example":"Contoh: Frances’ book; James’ hat","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_possessives-of-proper-names-ending-in-s-style_option_add-apostrophe-s_example":"Contoh: Frances’s book; James’s hat","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_possessives-of-proper-names-ending-in-s-style_option_add-apostrophe-s_name":"Gunakan tanda apostrof dan \"s\"","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_possessives-of-proper-names-ending-in-s-style_option_add-apostrophe-only_name":"Gunakan hanya tanda apostrof.","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_plus-sign-usage_name":"Jangan gunakan tanda plus untuk berarti \"dan\", kecuali jika tanda tersebut merupakan bagian dari nama sendiri.","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_comma-after-short-introductory-phrase_name":"Koma setelah frasa pengantar yang singkat","item_form_field_en_punctuation-v2_ampersand-abbreviation-spacing_option_use-spaces-before-and-after-ampersand-as-part-of-abbreviation_name":"Gunakan spasi","item_form_field_en_numbers-v2_units-of-measure-spacing_option_use-space-between-numeral-and-unit-of-measure_example":"Contoh: 10 MB; 5 kg","item_form_field_en_numbers-v2_units-of-measure-spacing_option_do-not-use-space-between-numeral-and-unit-of-measure_name":"Jangan gunakan spasi antara angka dan satuan.","item_form_field_en_numbers-v2_spelling-out-units_name":"Satuan ukuran","item_form_field_fr_numbers-v2_spelling-out-units_name":"Saat menulis satuan ukuran","item_form_field_es_numbers-v2_spelling-out-units_name":"Saat menulis satuan ukuran","item_form_field_ko_numbers-v2_spelling-out-units_name":"Satuan ukuran","item_form_field_it_numbers-v2_spelling-out-units_name":"Satuan ukuran","item_form_field_ja_numbers-v2_spelling-out-units_name":"Unit","item_form_field_en_numbers-v2_units-of-measure-spacing_option_use-space-between-numeral-and-unit-of-measure_name":"Gunakan spasi antara angka dan satuan.","item_form_field_en_numbers-v2_thousands-separator_option_use-space-to-separate-large-numbers-into-units-of-three_name":"Gunakan spasi untuk memisahkan angka besar menjadi tiga bagian","item_form_field_en_numbers-v2_list-of-measurements-with-units_name":"Untuk 2 atau lebih pengukuran, seperti dalam rentang, seri, atau dimensi, gunakan angka dan satuan yang disingkat.","item_form_field_en_numbers-v2_large-sums-of-money-format_name":"Menulis jumlah uang yang besar","item_form_field_it_numbers-v2_large-sums-of-money_name":"Menulis jumlah uang yang besar","item_form_field_en_numbers-v2_thousands-separator_option_use-comma-to-separate-large-numbers-into-units-of-three_name":"Gunakan koma untuk memisahkan angka besar menjadi tiga bagian","item_form_field_es_numbers-v2_decimal-separator_name":"Untuk memisahkan desimal","item_form_field_en_numbers-v2_dimensions-separator_option_use-x-between-dimensions-without-space-on-either-side_example":"Contoh: 1200 x 1800; 13 x 7,5 x 4","item_form_field_en_numbers-v2_dimensions-separator_option_use-x-between-dimensions-without-space-on-either-side_name":"Gunakan huruf kecil \"